HOL Light
---------

Upstream: https://github.com/jrh13/hol-light
License: BSD-2-Clause-like terms; complete notice in LICENSES/HOL-Light.txt.

The whole rhombus-hol-kernel package is conservatively distributed subject to
the HOL Light notice. The closest correspondences are htype.rhm, term.rhm, and
kernel.rhm. In rhombus-hol-lib, the notice also covers conv.rhm, drule.rhm,
algebra.rhm, infinity.rhm, wfrec.rhm, treerep.rhm, datatype construction code,
and their tests and documentation. These files adapt the type/term structure,
primitive rules, conversions, derived rules, pair/sum/natural-number
constructions, and well-founded recursion techniques of HOL Light.
The Isabelle formalization is second-generation correspondence code for that
kernel and is conservatively covered by the same notice.

HOL4
----

Upstream: https://github.com/HOL-Theorem-Prover/HOL
License: BSD-3-Clause; complete notice in LICENSES/HOL4.txt.

The HOL4 notice conservatively covers bool.rhm and related base-logic tests and
documentation, which follow HOL4's choice of logical constants and ETA,
SELECT, and BOOL_CASES axioms, and any HOL4-derived parts of the recursive
function construction.
The Isabelle base-logic and model theories are conservatively covered by the
same HOL4 notice.

ACL2
----

Upstream: https://github.com/acl2/acl2
License: BSD-3-Clause; complete notice in LICENSES/ACL2.txt.

The ACL2 notice conservatively covers the automatic prover implementation,
including waterfall.rhm, goal.rhm, simp.rhm, destruct.rhm, fertilize.rhm,
general.rhm, irrelevance.rhm, induct.rhm, order.rhm, ruledb.rhm, and the ACL2-
style hint handling in elab.rhm and driver.rhm, together with related tests and
documentation. These files adapt ACL2's waterfall organization, term ordering,
rule behavior, type-prescription use, and proof hints to an LCF-style HOL
kernel.

